  "note": "Re-judged 2026-10-24 (independent auditor, authored none of 9c3697d0d1). RFC 8654 Section 3: \"Peers that wish to use the BGP Extended Message Capability MUST support error handling for BGP UPDATE messages per [RFC7606].\" The only change to TestRFC8654ExtendedDuplicateMPResets is its MUTATION comment naming ValidateUpdateRFC7606Peer instead of the deleted ValidateUpdateRFC7606AddPath. Re-read the body: on a session with Extended Message, a single MP_REACH and a single MP_UNREACH in a >4096-octet UPDATE stay Established with the exact body dispatched once; the duplicate gives an error, Idle, no further dispatch and NOTIFICATION 3/1 with empty data. Positive and negative are distinct phases. Producer ValidateUpdateRFC7606Peer's duplicate-MP reset unchanged in behavior. Other carriers unchanged. FINDING still open from the previous judgement: the positive tag on TestRFC8654ExtendedMessageSessionUsesRFC7606ErrorHandling names the malformed-ORIGIN subtest, an error input, so that unit is two negatives; fix: retag it as a second negative, or add a well-formed over-4096 subtest asserting dispatch with attributes and NLRI intact and move the positive tag there. Conforming positives come from the other units. Units ran green at HEAD.",
